  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 7-Angeloylechinatine and the CD276 antigen, mediated through the Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This pathway is supported by two distinct but overlapping routes: one involving 7-Angeloylechinatine directly targeting the Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, and another where 7-Angeloylechinatine acts on Agallochin F, which in turn targets the CD276 antigen. Both routes share the common intermediate of the Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, indicating a possible shared mechanism of action. The scores from the two paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between 7-Angeloylechinatine and CD276, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the role of the intermediate proteins.",
